# NOTICE

## Leyline (chat presentation layer)

This workbench reuses and modifies parts of Leyline:

- Upstream: https://github.com/spmurrayzzz/leyline
- Pinned commit: `a368c8b7590b88bb138c024b7dd8414b3dcc2a73`
- License: Apache-2.0 (`src/vendor/leyline/LICENSE`)

Reused files and modifications:

- `src/styles/tokens.css`, `transcript.css`, `tools.css`, `composer.css`:
  copied from `src/styles/`. The Pi workbench adds `workbench.css` and overrides
  message-row surfaces; unused Leyline application rules are harmless.
- `src/projection/toolStatus.ts`: derived from `lib/tool-activity.js`
  (`toolStatusTone`) and rewritten for the finite Pi tool status set.
- `src/components/TranscriptEntry.vue`: rewritten and trimmed from
  `src/components/TranscriptEntry.vue`; the tool/skill/thinking card structure
  and class names are retained. Research, subagent inspector, terminal, Git,
  fork/reset and other capabilities without a Pi host equivalent were removed.
- `src/components/AskUserForm.vue` and `ApprovalCard.vue`: new Vue components for
  this project; the AskUser interaction shape is informed by the community
  comparison research, not copied from a Leyline runtime.

Not reused: Leyline's Node server, Pi SDK runtime, WebSocket protocol, Electron
shell, project/machine/workspace features, terminal, Git, memory, tracing
services and extension confirm UI.

Extraction boundary evidence: Leyline's chat assembly lives in a ~5,800-line
`App.vue` and its session controller (`useSessionWorkspace.js`, ~2,000 lines)
is directly coupled to REST/WS project and machine APIs. That is beyond the v2
boundary (no community backend, no project/workspace model), so this workbench
kept the reusable presentation primitives (card markup/classes, styles,
status mapping, Markdown/scroll behavior) and wrote a contract-specific
transcript/controller instead of forking the whole shell. This is a deliberate,
recorded adaptation rather than a claim that the original container was moved
unchanged.

